  ---
  Data + Metadata Flow

  WRITE (Databricks)
  ──────────────────
  1. Spark writes parquet files → ADLS
  2. Delta transaction log updated → ADLS
  3. UniForm generates Iceberg metadata → ADLS
  4. Unity Catalog registers table metadata

  READ (Snowflake)
  ────────────────
  1. Snowflake calls UC REST endpoint → gets latest snapshot
  2. Snowflake reads Iceberg metadata → ADLS
  3. Snowflake reads parquet files → ADLS
  4. Returns query results

  ---
  Key Design Principles

  ✅ One copy of data        — parquet files in ADLS, read by both engines
  ✅ Open format             — Iceberg, not proprietary
  ✅ No vendor lock-in       — swap Snowflake for any Iceberg engine
  ✅ No secrets              — Access Connector (managed identity)
  ✅ No REFRESH needed       — Snowflake reads live from UC REST
  ✅ No Snowflake Connector  — pure Iceberg protocol
  ✅ Serverless capable      — no cluster JAR management
  ✅ Same region             — no cross-region egress costs

  ---
  IAM Summary

  dbx-access-connector → ADLS
    Storage Blob Data Contributor      (read/write data files)
    Storage Account Contributor        (manage storage)
    Storage Queue Data Contributor     (file events)

  Snowflake Managed Identity → ADLS
    Storage Blob Data Contributor      (read metadata + data)
    Storage Blob Delegator             (user delegation keys)

  dbx-access-connector → Azure Subscription
    EventGrid EventSubscription Contributor

  ---
  What Each Engine Does

  Databricks                    Snowflake
  ──────────────────────        ──────────────────────────
  WRITES data                   READS data
  Owns the write path           Owns the query/analytics path
  Uses Unity Catalog            Uses Catalog Integration
  Delta + UniForm format        Pure Iceberg reader
  Serverless compute            Serverless warehouse
  No Snowflake dependency       No Databricks dependency

  ---
  One Line Summary

  ▎ Databricks writes Delta+Iceberg files to ADLS via Unity Catalog. Snowflake reads the same files as Iceberg via UC REST endpoint. One dataset, two engines, zero connectors, zero data duplication.
